"""
A replaced element is INLINE-LEVEL: it sits on a line box beside text and its
BOTTOM MARGIN EDGE rests on that line's baseline (CSS 2.1 §10.8.1, "the
baseline of an inline replaced element is the bottom margin edge").

Round 18 gave `<audio>`, `<video>`, `<canvas>`, `<embed>`, `<object>` and
`<iframe>` their correct UA default BOXES and left their POSITIONS wrong, and
said so in its own "What is left" item 1: this renderer still laid them out as
block-level, stacking them one per row. The measured oracle for that claim,
harvested by `scripts/check/check-chrome-layout-geometry-diff.shs` from Chrome
152 on the `animation` catalog page:

    Chrome  path:0/0/2 | canvas | x= 45 | y=295 | 120 |  40 | display=inline
    Chrome  path:0/0/3 | svg    | x=169 | y=295 | 120 |  40 | display=inline
    Chrome  path:0/0/4 | audio  | x=294 | y=281 | 300 |  54 | display=inline
    Chrome  path:0/0/5 | video  | x=594 | y=185 | 120 | 150 | display=inline

All four bottom out at exactly 335 — one line box, four boxes of four
different heights sitting on one baseline. Simple (Run A of round 19) gets
every WIDTH and HEIGHT right and every POSITION wrong:

    diff    path:0/0/2 | canvas | dx=  0 dy=110 dw=0 dh=0
    diff    path:0/0/3 | svg    | dx=124 dy= 70 dw=0 dh=0
    diff    path:0/0/4 | audio  | dx=249 dy= 16 dw=0 dh=0
    diff    path:0/0/5 | video  | dx=549 dy=134 dw=0 dh=0

and the whole rest of the page rides 126-128 px low behind them.

The cause is a routing gap, not a layout-loop gap — the same shape as all three
of round 18's items. `is_inline_tag` (the hardcoded UA `display` table at
`simple_web_html_layout_renderer_style.spl`) carries no replaced tag at all, so
each of these fell through to the BLOCK path. The machinery to place them
correctly already existed and had never run: the inline height clamp in
`layout_with_style` carries an explicit `grid_item_is_replaced` exclusion whose
comment names `img`, and with no replaced tag ever reaching `display:inline`
that exclusion was unreachable code.

MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED — three premises were checked against the harvested
Chrome geometry before any edit, and two of them came back different from what
the round-18 hand-off predicted:

  * `<input>`, `<select>`, `<textarea>` and `<button>` are `display:inline-BLOCK`
    in Chrome, not `inline` (census over all eight `*.geom.txt`). They are
    therefore NOT given `display:inline` here. `<input>` and `<select>` are in
    fact `inline` in this engine today and that is a separate defect, recorded
    in the round-19 metrics doc rather than fixed blind: an inline-block form
    control aligns on its INNER TEXT baseline, not its bottom margin edge, so
    flipping it would move it by its padding and border and needs its own
    measurement.
  * the eight-page catalog contains NO `<img>` and NO `<iframe>` at all, so no
    Chrome row measures either one. `<img>` is still added to the inline table —
    HTML's UA sheet is unambiguous and the exclusion comment already names it —
    but it is asserted here only on what is unambiguous (it is inline-level, it
    honours its `width`/`height` attributes on their own axes). No 300x150
    default is invented for it: that number is not measured anywhere in this
    catalog, and `replaced_default_box_w("img")` deliberately stays 0.

SABOTAGE (run before landing, with `grep -c SABOTAGED` first — round 18's trap
was a sed that silently did not apply): drop `tag == "canvas"` from
`is_inline_tag` and AC-1/AC-2/AC-3 must fail while the `<span>`, `<div>` and
`display:block`-override controls stay green; separately, make
`inline_line_baseline_ascent` return the font strut for a replaced box instead
of its bottom margin edge and AC-3 alone must fail, proving AC-3 measures the
baseline rule and not merely "they are on one line".
"""

"""
Traceability: REQ-BROWSER-ENGINE-REPLACED-003 — replaced elements are inline-level boxes that share a line box with text and align their bottom margin edge to the line's baseline.
"""
# @cover src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/browser_engine/simple_web_html_layout_renderer_layout.spl 1%
use std.spec.*
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.simple_web_html_layout_renderer.{
    simple_web_layout_debug_layout_by_id
}
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.simple_web_html_layout_renderer_style.{
    is_inline_tag
}
use std.gc_async_mut.gpu.browser_engine.simple_web_html_layout_renderer_layout.{
    replaced_default_box_w, replaced_media_bottom_edge_tag
}

val VW: i32 = 900
val VH: i32 = 20000
val HEAD: text = "<html><head><style>*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;font:16px/1.5 sans-serif}#wrap{width:810px;margin:0;padding:0}</style></head><body><div id=\"wrap\">"

fn probe(inner: text, id: text, prop: text) -> i32:
    val out = simple_web_layout_debug_layout_by_id(
        HEAD + inner + "</div></body></html>", VW, VH, id, prop)
    parse_int(out)

# Two 120x40 canvases with NO whitespace between them, so the pen advance is
# the first box's width exactly and nothing has to be allowed for a space.
val TWO_BOXES: text = "<canvas id=\"a\" width=\"120\" height=\"40\"></canvas><canvas id=\"b\" width=\"120\" height=\"40\"></canvas>"

describe "a replaced element is an inline-level box on the line":
    it "AC-1: a canvas after text stays on the SAME line, not below it":
        step("animation page: Chrome canvas x=45 (line start); Simple stacked it as a block")
        val x = probe("<span id=\"t\">hi</span><canvas id=\"a\" width=\"120\" height=\"40\"></canvas>", "a", "x")
        expect(x > 0).to_equal(true)

    it "AC-2: two adjacent replaced boxes sit side by side on one line":
        step("Chrome: canvas x=45 then svg x=169 then audio x=294 then video x=594")
        val ax = probe(TWO_BOXES, "a", "x")
        val aw = probe(TWO_BOXES, "a", "w")
        val bx = probe(TWO_BOXES, "b", "x")
        val ay = probe(TWO_BOXES, "a", "y")
        val by = probe(TWO_BOXES, "b", "y")
        expect(bx).to_equal(ax + aw)
        expect(by).to_equal(ay)

    it "AC-3: unequal-height replaced boxes share ONE baseline at their bottom edges":
        step("Chrome bottoms: canvas 295+40, audio 281+54, video 185+150 = 335 for all three")
        val inner = "<canvas id=\"a\" width=\"120\" height=\"40\"></canvas><video id=\"v\"></video>"
        val a_bottom = probe(inner, "a", "y") + probe(inner, "a", "h")
        val v_bottom = probe(inner, "v", "y") + probe(inner, "v", "h")
        expect(a_bottom).to_equal(v_bottom)

    it "AC-4: a tall replaced box grows the line box so the next block clears it":
        step("a 150 px video must push the following <p> below 150, not below one 24 px line")
        val inner = "<video id=\"v\"></video><p id=\"p\">after</p>"
        val v_bottom = probe(inner, "v", "y") + probe(inner, "v", "h")
        expect(probe(inner, "p", "y") >= v_bottom).to_equal(true)

    it "AC-5 (control): display:block on the same element still stacks it":
        step("a UA default that could not be overridden by author CSS would be a regression")
        val inner = "<span id=\"t\">hi</span><canvas id=\"a\" style=\"display:block\" width=\"120\" height=\"40\"></canvas>"
        expect(probe(inner, "a", "x")).to_equal(0)

    it "AC-6 (control): <div> is untouched and remains a full-width block":
        step("the inline table must not have widened to non-replaced block tags")
        val inner = "<span id=\"t\">hi</span><div id=\"d\">x</div>"
        expect(probe(inner, "d", "x")).to_equal(0)
        expect(probe(inner, "d", "w")).to_equal(810)

    it "AC-7 (control): <span> was already inline and does not move":
        step("round 17/18 inline behaviour must be preserved exactly")
        val inner = "<span id=\"s\">hi</span>"
        expect(probe(inner, "s", "x")).to_equal(0)
        expect(probe(inner, "s", "h")).to_equal(18)

    it "AC-8: <img> is inline-level and honours width/height on their own axes":
        step("no <img> exists in the catalog, so only the unambiguous part is asserted")
        val inner = "<span id=\"t\">hi</span><img id=\"m\" width=\"120\" height=\"40\">"
        expect(probe(inner, "m", "x") > 0).to_equal(true)
        expect(probe(inner, "m", "w")).to_equal(120)
        expect(probe(inner, "m", "h")).to_equal(40)

    it "AC-9: every tag with a UA replaced default box is routed inline":
        step("a replaced default box that is never reached from the inline path is unreachable code")
        var missing = ""
        for t in ["iframe", "video", "canvas", "embed", "object", "audio"]:
            if replaced_default_box_w(t) > 0 and not is_inline_tag(t):
                missing = missing + t + " "
        expect(missing).to_equal("")

    it "AC-11 (control): the bottom-edge baseline is scoped to replaced MEDIA":
        step("<select>/<input> are in grid_item_is_replaced AND are display:inline in this")
        step("engine, so an unscoped predicate caught them — measured: form_control_widget")
        step("_box_spec AC-6 (<label>Choice <select>…) went 33 -> 39 px before this scoping.")
        var leaked = ""
        for t in ["input", "select", "textarea", "button", "progress", "meter"]:
            if replaced_media_bottom_edge_tag(t):
                leaked = leaked + t + " "
        var missing = ""
        for t in ["img", "svg", "video", "audio", "canvas", "iframe", "embed", "object"]:
            if not replaced_media_bottom_edge_tag(t):
                missing = missing + t + " "
        expect(leaked).to_equal("")
        expect(missing).to_equal("")

    it "AC-10 (control): form controls are NOT given display:inline by this table":
        step("Chrome reports input/select/textarea/button as inline-BLOCK; measured, not assumed")
        var wrong = ""
        for t in ["input", "select", "textarea", "button"]:
            if is_inline_tag(t):
                wrong = wrong + t + " "
        expect(wrong).to_equal("")
